      "message": "You can delete the line. The test should still pass, because the encoder applying offsets from the specified CQ levels to derive first and second frame QPs still results in valid encoded output. A similar thing applies to switching from tune IQ to SSIM.\n\nOne thing worth mentioning: by deleting the line, the test might lose some of its regression testing capabilities. This will still test a valid scenario, but not under the same conditions it was originally written for. Given that this is a release branch (with a self-limiting number of new commits vs. main), I think deleting the line vs. doing anything more sophisticated is worth it.",
